WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
have you ever wondered what iconic  twilight scenes would look like  if movie magic hadn't interfered without  the help of cgi  many of our favorite franchises most  iconic scenes would look  pretty silly twilight is no exception  with all the fantastical fight scenes  drastic aging of characters throughout  the films  and many actors seeming to seamlessly  transition from human to werewolf  let's break down how some of the  twilight franchise's famous scenes were  brought to life  in twilight one of the hallmark traits  of a vampire  is their glittering skin when it catches  the sunlight that's like diamonds  ilm the special effects team also owned  by lucasfilm  was able to add in the extra sparkle on  pattinson's face  in post-production in new moon prime  focus vfx was responsible for making  edward sparkle  visual effects supervisor eric  pascarelli explains the process  there was a very delicate balance of the  elements that make up the effect  we use 3d particle geometry dispersed  over a cg model of edward's head to  reflect several artificial environments  in order to create the sparkles and rays  one of the most romantic and  exhilarating moments for bella early on  in the relationship  is jumping through trees with edward you  better hold on tight spider monkey  in the movie it looks easy enough but  sparing no expense  the producers of twilight didn't want to  only rely on cgi for these moments  the visual effects team led by richard  kidd had to install  a support rig that was about 100 feet  tall and spanning three large pine trees  it was four pipes that created the  structure like a box  and they snap together like lego pieces  kids said  the rig wasn't only for studying the  natural pine trees but also used to hold  the winches and pulleys used to carry  the actors and crew  up and down from the trees once the  filming was finished  the visual effects team had to go back  and digitally remove the rig  cables and harness used on the actors  which required a lot of meticulous work  on the editor's end  generally considered sombre films the  twilight series offers moments of levity  the vampire baseball scene in the first  twilight movie is a great example  vampire baseball is just like regular  baseball  but a lot cooler to make the actors seem  as if they were practically flying they  were attached to a harness that would  move them around  in correlation to their marks the cast  also had to strut on a grass-covered  moving walkway to give the illusion of a  supernaturally speedy  vampire gate nobody can't forget that  epic  moment when we got to see jacob  transform from a teenager to a full-on  werewolf  while looking effortless practically  graceful on screen  there was a lot of work that went into  each of those transformations  the giant werewolves were all created  using cgi  and actor taylor lautner's already  filmed scenes were used for reference  launtner was hooked up to a harness to  simulate him jumping off into werewolf  form  and then a werewolf was built around  that and then added into the movie in  post-production  we all love bella for her quiet nature  open heart  and overall relatability but we also  love her because she's a strong woman  who sticks up for herself  we see in a scene in new moon a heated  confrontation about jacob  ends in bella punching paul making him  turn into his werewolf form  at first glance the scene looks like a  pretty easy one  but actress kristen stewart had to  rehearse that punch with a stunt  coordinator  and then coordinate the timing and the  moves out with the other actors  this scene also showed the audience  another graceful transformation from  human to werewolf by paul  eclipse has one of the most thrilling  and epic action scenes in the entire  franchise  the chase scene with victoria to  simulate jumping off of rocks  the actors were hooked up to a harness  attached to the ceiling of a filming  studio  where they would have to jump on green  screen boulders that were just green  ledges and steps  the actors were also filmed running on  what the production crew  called magic carpets that would make it  appear that they were running a lot  faster than they actually were  a tender moment shared between bella and  jacob in werewolf form  is right before the big battle scene  against victoria and her newborns  against the cullens and the werewolves  in eclipse  in the movie werewolf jacobs saddles up  to bella and she gives him a sweet  scratch on the head  which was all edited in post-production  to look like she was scratching a real  werewolf  while filming actor taylor lautner was  dressed in a non-reflective bodysuit and  hat  and he stood in where his werewolf self  would be in the movie  kristen stewart went as far as  scratching taylor's head while filming  werewolf or human in a bodysuit it's  still pretty sweet  the way the production staff were able  to make it seem like actress mackenzie  foy was  actually riding on the back of jacob in  werewolf form  is pretty complicated they had mackenzie  sit on a motion control rig  a machine that resembles a mechanical  bull with a saddle covered in werewolf  jacob's fur  the rig was set against a green screen  and pre-programmed with all the moves to  resemble jacob running  and mackenzie sat on it while they  filmed her with a wind machine blowing  so it looked like she was moving fast  the animators at tipit studio started by  going to the actual lumber yard and  getting footage there  then built the whole scene starting with  the dialogue from the actors from a  recording  tippit studios actually had helicopters  flown over the area with cameras so they  could get an  aerial view then they created a  storyboard deciding the shots  and once they were approved to move  forward they started working on  animating the wolves against the  real-life lumber yard backdrop  baby renesme was originally meant to be  a to scale animatronic doll  but the producers deemed it too scary to  use  and the actors never looked comfortable  acting against it  the animatronic version had full length  hair and giant  unnatural looking eyes even for a half  vampire half human  instead the producers decided to use cgi  a rubber baby doll and an actual human  baby to create  every aspect of baby resume which has  garnered better  but not great reviews from fans and  audiences alike  there were several options on how the  production team could choose to make  renesme age at a superhuman rate in  breaking dawn part 2  and they chose to use lola visual  effects to reimagine mckenzie as  renesmee from birth up until her age at  the end of the series  utilizing baby photos of mackenzie the  effects team was able to create an  accurate chart of what renesme would  look like at any age  and they used actual babies as physical  stand-ins while  shooting sounds pretty intense but the  payoff was worth it  the twilight saga and snow go together  like peanut butter and jelly in fans  minds  and it's fitting that the final battle  with the volturi is beautifully set with  a snow-capped background  but when actually filming the actors and  crew were inside a production studio  where there were green screen backdrops  and  fake snow grounds the camera crew rode  on a vehicle  while the actors had to run towards or  away from it in the snow  the pregnancy and eventual birth scenes  in the breaking dawn movies were one of  the few times we really got to  experience the horror and romance  aspects at its peak in twilight  to make kristen stewart look as  emancipated and frail as she did in the  movie  she went through extensive makeup and  even face prosthetics to really give the  full look  also the fx team actually built a  life-sized doll of kristen that they  used when edward was giving her cpr  kristen's actual body was underneath the  bed with the dummy on top  the final battle in eclipse is visually  breathtaking  seeing beautiful powerful people and  werewolves run around  in a snow-covered forest definitely  gives viewers a treat  believe it or not the battle in the snow  was filmed inside of a production studio  where a full-size set of the forest was  built where they couldn't use practical  effects  such as trees and fake snow a green  screen behind the set was utilized in  post-production to give it that winter  wonderland feel  one of the first times bella and the  audience gets to witness some of  edward's supernatural abilities  are in the intense action scene where  bella is almost hit by tyler's van  thankfully edward who was across the  parking lot sped to her rescue and  stopped the moving van with his hand  leaving a sizable dent they were able to  make this happen by replacing the  original passenger side door with a soft  molded door that would easily move under  robert pattinson's hand  we think those scenes are still iconic  with or without the green screens and  harnesses being visible  and we can't imagine the twilight  franchise without them  what do you think do the twilight movies  still maintain their magic  even without all the supernatural cgi  and fx added in by hollywood  let us know in the comments

